[all_together_top] parent=Whole Paper sample=7 attempt=1/7
Here is the list of contents in plain text format:

1. Random-Access Ranked Retrieval (RAR)
   - Algorithm based on geometric arrangements with logarithmic query time but exponential space complexity
   - Proposed space-efficient algorithms using \ud835\udf00-samples for stripe-range retrieval

2. Reduced RAR to RAS
3. Similarity Search Setting
   - Reduction described in Section 3.4
   - Lifting data points during preprocessing and applying the same lifting to the query at query time
   - Treating the query as a linear scoring function corresponding to the standard dot product

4. Baseline Methods for RAS
   - Quickselect algorithm for order statistics computation
   - Faiss library algorithms: HNSW, PQ, IVFPQ, IVFFlat, LSH

5. Experimental Results
   - Comparing query time and recall@i on random-access similarity search task
   - Evaluating the proposed algorithm EpsHier with other baseline methods
